      "title": "Director of Human Resources -",
      "description": "Director of Human Resources - Director of Human Resources - Kiosk mode Director of Human Resources Administrative Professional Regular Full Time Closing at: Sep 23 2027 - 23:55 EDT Add to favorites View favorites Title: Director of Human Resources VP Area: Finance & Operations Department: Published Salary Range: 70000-80000 Job Summary/Basic Function: Reporting to the Vice President for Finance and Operations, the Director of Human Resources is responsible for leadership and direction of the human resources and payroll functions of the university, regulatory compliance including Title IX, and campus safety. The Director leads a team with responsibility for HR programs, services, policies, and practices that support institutional priorities, culture, organizational effectiveness, and compliance. The successful candidate will ensure that the human resources team delivers high-quality customer service, demonstrates expertise in matters important to the recruitment, retention, and support of faculty and staff, establishes policies and procedures essential to university personnel operations, and manages HR and payroll data effectively. Additional oversight includes the campus safety office and Title IX coordinator to ensure the overall safety and security of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Responsible for designing, developing, and implementing all human resources management functions. Partner with leadership in achieving the mission and goals of the University. Review tools, approval workflows, and job functions within the office of human resources and make necessary changes to improve the effectiveness of the unit. Establish a culture that encourages teamwork, pride in employee roles, professional growth, and development in support of the institution’s mission and vision. Ensure excellent customer service in both internal and external relationships with the office. Responsible for managing employment status change related activities. Respo