      "title": "Fall & Spring 26'-27' Student Worker Trades",
      "description": "Fall & Spring 26'-27' Student Worker Trades - Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Fall & Spring 26'-27' Student Worker Trades - Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Fall & Spring 26'-27' Student Worker Trades Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Student Regular Part Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Fall & Spring 26'-27' Student Worker Trades VP Area: Finance & Operations Department: Facilities Management Published Salary Range: $13.73 Job Summary/Basic Function: Are you a hands on learner looking to gain valuable trades skills while earning money during the summer? Lake Superior State University's Facilities management team is seeking motivated student workers for our Summer 2026 semester. As a student worker in Trades, you'll work alongside experienced professionals maintaining our beautiful campus. Your responsibilities will include assisting the Trades department and with maintenance and construction services for assigned buildings around campus. Minimum Qualifications: Currently enrolled LSSU student Self-Motivated individuals who enjoy problem-solving Interest in developing practical trades skills Strong Work Ethic and attention to safety Physical Demands: Some Heavy Lifting may be required ( 50lbs or more) Work Hours: Monday - Friday; Up to 19 hours per week with Flexible scheduling Apply now! Similar Jobs Regional Recruiter Admissions • Serve as the primary LSSU admissions representative for the assigned regional territory. • Recruit prospective freshmen, transfer, and non-traditional students through high school visits, community college visits, college fairs, and community events. • Build and maintain positive relationships with high school counselors, community college advisors, alumni, and community organizations to promote LSSU. • Conduct individual advising sessions, group presentations, and information sessions to guide students and families through the admissions and financial aid process. • Act