    "https://jobs.lssu.edu/jobs/2026-2027-ncaa-sports-technical-director": {
      "title": "2026-2027 NCAA Sports Technical Director -",
      "description": "2026-2027 NCAA Sports Technical Director - 2026-2027 NCAA Sports Technical Director - Kiosk mode 2026-2027 NCAA Sports Technical Director Administrative Professional Athletics Temporary Part Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: 2026-2027 NCAA Sports Technical Director VP Area: Athletics Department: Athletics Published Salary Range: $30.00/hr Job Summary/Basic Function: Lake Superior State University Athletics is seeking a skilled and detail-oriented NCAA Sports Technical Director. Reporting directly to the Assistant Athletic Director for Game Management, this position is responsible for overseeing live in-venue production elements, jumbotron operations, and multi-media technical aspects of home athletic contests directly from the press box or scorers' table. The Technical Director ensures a high-quality, professional, and engaging game-day environment for student-athletes and fans while maintaining strict compliance with NCAA regulations. Key Responsibilities Jumbotron & Video Board Operation: Direct and manage the live in-arena video board production, including switching internal camera feeds, executing instant replays, playing institutional or sponsor graphics, and coordinating in-game crowd entertainment elements. Technical Game Management: Oversee the setup, operation, and teardown of press box and scorers' table technical systems, ensuring seamless integration of the official game clock, shot clocks, statistical software displays, and public address audio systems. Crew Leadership: Supervise, train, and coordinate student game-day staff assigned to technical roles, including scoreboard operators, replay technicians, camera operators, and audio engineers. Game Management Collaboration: Partner closely with the Assistant Athletic Director for Game Management and sports information staff to execute the pre-game script, timing protocols, and promotional activities flawlessly. Troubleshooting & Maintenance: Perform pre-game diagnostic checks on all stadium/arena A/V and production equipment. Rapidly troubleshoot technical glitches under live, high-pressure sports environments. Minimum Qualifications: Technical Skills: Proven experience operating professional video switchers, digital graphics software, and stadium audio consoles. Sports Knowledge: Strong familiarity with NCAA rules, timing structures, and statistical tracking across core university sports (specifically Ice Hockey, Basketball, and Volleyball). Availability: Ability to work a flexible schedule, including heavy evening, weekend, and select holiday hours aligned with the LSSU varsity athletic calendar. Characteristics: Exceptional communication skills, grace under pressure, strong leadership abilities, and acute attention to detail. Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience directing or technical-directing live in-arena entertainment or video boards at the collegiate or professional level. Familiarity with the integration of NCAA-approved statistics programs (e.g., Genius Sports, StatCrew) with in-stadium display systems. Physical Demands: Ability to remain stationary in a press box or at a scorers' table for extended periods during athletic contests. Sufficient manual dexterity to operate complex electronic switchboards, computers, and A/V gear. Occasional lifting and moving of production equipment up to 30 lbs Apply now! Similar Jobs Regional Recruiter Admissions • Serve as the primary LSSU admissions representative for the assigned regional territory. • Recruit prospective freshmen, transfer, and non-traditional students through high school visits, community college visits, college fairs, and community events. • Build and maintain positive relationships with high school counselors, community college advisors, alumni, and community organizations to promote LSSU. • Conduct individual advising sessions, group presentations, and information sessions to guide students and families through the admissions and financial aid process. • Actively manage territory through a strategic communication plan utilizing multiple platforms, including email, phone, text, social media, and CRM (Slate). • Regularly track and report outreach activities, prospect data, and enrollment trends to inform strategies and assess effectiveness. • Meet established recruitment goals, communication benchmarks, and enrollment targets for the assigned region. • Collaborate with the broader Admissions team to execute university-wide recruitment campaigns and special initiatives. • Organize and host local recruitment events and receptions for prospective and admitted students. • Travel to LSSU’s main campus at least once per quarter. • Other duties as assigned. Regional Recruiter Admissions • Serve as the primary LSSU admissions representative for the assigned regional territory. • Recruit prospective freshmen, transfer, and non-traditional students through high school visits, community college visits, college fairs, and community events. • Build and maintain positive relationships with high school counselors, community college advisors, alumni, and community organizations to promote LSSU. • Conduct individual advising sessions, group presentations, and information sessions to guide students and families through the admissions and financial aid process. • Actively manage territory through a strategic communication plan utilizing multiple platforms, including email, phone, text, social media, and CRM (Slate). • Regularly track and report outreach activities, prospect data, and enrollment trends to inform strategies and assess effectiveness. • Meet established recruitment goals, communication benchmarks, and enrollment targets for the assigned region. • Collaborate with the broader Admissions team to execute university-wide recruitment campaigns and special initiatives. • Organize and host local recruitment events and receptions for prospective and admitted students. • Travel to LSSU’s main campus at least once per quarter. • Other duties as assigned. Academic Accessibility Services Coordinator Library & Academic Services Work with faculty, staff, and external service providers to coordinate and implement services for students with disabilities. Review and establish reasonable accommodations for students under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act and the federal Fair Housing Act. Act as a resource for academic accessibility related information across all areas of campus. Maintain confidential cumulative records of all students served. Complete student intake process, determine eligibility, and arrange academic accommodations for eligible students. Responsible for providing and supporting adaptive technology and auxiliary aids when applicable (such as assistive technologies including; alternative format textbooks, screen reading programs, assistive hearing or vision devices, assistive software, and other supports as appropriate). Develop and update Academic Accessibility Services policies and procedures as needed. Serve as liaison to Housing and Student Life on issues related to students with disabilities to ensure compliance with ADA and the Fair Housing Act. Work collaboratively with the Office of Housing and Residence Life to receive and recommend Housing, Dining and/or Service/Assistance Animal accommodation requests. Maintain up-to-date knowledge on best practices and issues in the field. Participate in relevant professional development activities to stay informed of state and federal regulations regarding students with disabilities and special populations. Keep staff and administration informed of state and federal requirements for areas of assigned responsibility. Coordinate services for students with temporary disabilities. Represent Academic Accessibility Services at campus events. Serve on campus committees and is active in professional organizations. Serve as an active and collaborative member of the Library & Academic Services team. Perform other duties as assigned. Director of Human Resources Reporting to the Vice President for Finance and Operations, the Director of Human Resources is responsible for leadership and direction of the human resources and payroll functions of the university, regulatory compliance including Title IX, and campus safety. The Director leads a team with responsibility for HR programs, services, policies, and practices that support institutional priorities, culture, organizational effectiveness, and compliance. The successful candidate will ensure that the human resources team delivers high-quality customer service, demonstrates expertise in matters important to the recruitment, retention, and support of faculty and staff, establishes policies and procedures essential to university personnel operations, and manages HR and payroll data effectively. Additional oversight includes the campus safety office and Title IX coordinator to ensure the overall safety and security of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Economics Adjunct Instructor - MBA Program College of Business, Engineering, Computer Science, & Mathematics Lake Superior State University (LSSU) is seeking a dedicated individual to develop and deliver course content for ECON 645 (Economics for Managers) as part of our Master of Business Administration Program. The course will be offered online using Moodle from October 19 to December 11, 2026. As one of LSSU’s core values is excellence in teaching and learning, the successful candidate will contribute to the institution’s educational mission by prioritizing student-centered learning and fostering a welcoming and inclusive academic environment for all. We seek applicants who are passionate about meeting students where they are and guiding them toward success. LSSU is a student-focused institution known for small class sizes, engaged faculty, and real-world learning. Our academic programs emphasize experiential education, preparing students to lead and innovate in their fields. 2026-2027 Game Operations Student Staff Lake Superior State University Athletics is seeking dependable and enthusiastic students to join the Game Day Operations Team. These essential roles support the execution of home athletic events for Laker Hockey, Volleyball, and Men’s and Women’s Basketball, ensuring a professional and entertaining experience for student-athletes, fans, and visitors. Key Responsibilities: Students may be assigned one or more of the following roles depending on availability, experience, and interest: 1. Scoreboard & Time Clock Operator Operate the game clock, scoreboard, shot clock, and penalty timers using official systems, Work closely with officials and scorekeepers to ensure accurate timing and display, Maintain focus and attention to detail throughout the game. 2. Technical Assistant Assist with technical aspects including lighting, jumbotron operation and sound support 5. On-Ice / On-Court Support Set up and tear down game equipment (e.g., nets, scorer’s tables, signage, warm-up areas). Support intermission and timeout activities Help with managing benches, locker room access, and team logistics. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) e552c5c4 Last Name (required) 004f61a2 Email (required) cf98df87 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details"
