    "https://jobs.lssu.edu/jobs/adjunct-instructor-of-business": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Business -",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Business - Adjunct Instructor of Business - Kiosk mode Adjunct Instructor of Business Adjunct Adjunct Title: Adjunct Instructor of Business VP Area: Academic Affairs Department: College of Professional Studies Job Summary/Basic Function: Lake Superior State University invites applicants for adjunct faculty positions in a variety of business disciplines in the Lukenda School of Business. As one of LSSU’s core values is excellence in teaching and learning, the successful candidate will contribute to the institution’s educational mission by prioritizing student-centered learning and fostering a welcoming and inclusive academic environment for all. We seek applicants who are passionate about meeting students where they are and guiding them toward success. Lake Superior State University is a student-focused institution known for small class sizes, engaged faculty, and real-world learning. Our academic programs emphasize experiential education, preparing students to lead and innovate in their fields. Nestled in the scenic Upper Peninsula of Michigan near the Canadian border, LSSU offers a unique blend of natural beauty, community engagement, and academic experiences—making it a special place to live, work, and learn. Minimum Qualifications: -Masters Degree in a business-related field. -Ability to teach undergraduate students through engaging instruction. -Commitment to fostering an inclusive, student-centered academic environment. Preferred Qualifications: -DBA or Ph.D. in a business-related field -3 or more years of experience teaching at the undergraduate level. -Research experience. Physical Demands: Ability to manage and deliver instruction for a course over a semester, including timely communication and grading. Additional Information The Lukenda School of Business values excellence in teaching and research, supports innovation in classroom instruction, and prioritizes meaningful student engagement. Learn more about our department: https://www.lssu.edu/lukenda-school-of-business/ . Employment is contingent upon eligibility to work in the U.S. by the effective date of the appointment and successful completion of a background check. For additional information, contact Mindy McCready, Dean of the College of Professional Studies at mmccready2@lssu.edu. Review of applications is ongoing, and positions are filled as needed each semester. Special Instructions to Applicants: Submit a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Apply now! Similar Jobs Regional Recruiter Admissions • Serve as the primary LSSU admissions representative for the assigned regional territory. • Recruit prospective freshmen, transfer, and non-traditional students through high school visits, community college visits, college fairs, and community events. • Build and maintain positive relationships with high school counselors, community college advisors, alumni, and community organizations to promote LSSU. • Conduct individual advising sessions, group presentations, and information sessions to guide students and families through the admissions and financial aid process. • Actively manage territory through a strategic communication plan utilizing multiple platforms, including email, phone, text, social media, and CRM (Slate). • Regularly track and report outreach activities, prospect data, and enrollment trends to inform strategies and assess effectiveness. • Meet established recruitment goals, communication benchmarks, and enrollment targets for the assigned region. • Collaborate with the broader Admissions team to execute university-wide recruitment campaigns and special initiatives. • Organize and host local recruitment events and receptions for prospective and admitted students. • Travel to LSSU’s main campus at least once per quarter. • Other duties as assigned. Regional Recruiter Admissions • Serve as the primary LSSU admissions representative for the assigned regional territory. • Recruit prospective freshmen, transfer, an