    "https://jobs.lssu.edu/jobs/bus-driver-sault-ste-marie-michigan-united-states-5e0ef0c9-b03c-4993-a8b4-5d7adef55963": {
      "title": "Bus Driver",
      "description": "Bus Driver - Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Bus Driver - Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Bus Driver Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Administrative Professional Regular Part Time Title: Bus Driver VP Area: Academic Affairs Department: Charter Schools Office Published Salary Range: 26.50/HR Job Summary/Basic Function: Under the supervision of the LSSU Charter Schools designee, provide safe, reliable, and professional transportation services for university groups and contracted events. The drivers will be responsible for transporting students, staff, athletic teams, and other groups to various events, ensuring compliance with all Michigan licensing laws, University Risk and Safety policies, and OSHA safety standards. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Operate university-contracted buses and vans safely and professionally. Transport passengers reliably to scheduled destinations in a punctual manner. Perform vehicle inspections before and after trips as required. Adhere to all traffic laws, safety protocols, and university transportation policies. Maintain precise trip logs and mileage reports. Assist passengers with boarding and exiting as needed. Maintain the cleanliness and basic maintenance of assigned vehicles. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Valid Michigan Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) with Group B and Passenger (P) endorsement. 2. Clean driving record with no major violations and a background check. 3. Ability to successfully complete all necessary State of Michigan driving and safety examinations. 4. Must meet all OSHA and Department of Transportation (DOT) compliance standards. 5. Previous experience operating commercial buses or passenger vehicles. 6. Minimum age of 21 years old (following CDL passenger requirements). 7. Excellent communication and customer service skills. 8. Availability to work evenings, weekends, on-call shifts, and irregular schedules as required. Physical Demands: The above statement reflects the general duties considered necessary to describe the principal functions of the job identified and shall not be construed as a detailed description of all the work requirements that may be inherent in the job. It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct and control the work of employees under his/her supervision. Work Hours: Flexible Apply now! Similar Jobs Regional Recruiter Admissions • Serve as the primary LSSU admissions representative for the assigned regional territory. • Recruit prospective freshmen, transfer, and non-traditional students through high school visits, community college visits, college fairs, and community events. • Build and maintain positive relationships with high school counselors, community college advisors, alumni, and community organizations to promote LSSU. • Conduct individual advising sessions, group presentations, and information sessions to guide students and families through the admissions and financial aid process. • Actively manage territory through a strategic communication plan utilizing multiple platforms, including email, phone, text, social media, and CRM (Slate). • Regularly track and report outreach activities, prospect data, and enrollment trends to inform strategies and assess effectiveness. • Meet established recruitment goals, communication benchmarks, and enrollment targets for the assigned region. • Collaborate with the broader Admissions team to execute university-wide recruitment campaigns and special initiatives. • Organize and host local recruitment events and receptions for prospective and admitted students. • Travel to LSSU’s main campus at least once per quarter. • Other duties as assigned. Regional Recruiter Admissions • Serve as the primary LSSU admissions representative for the assigned regional territory. • Recruit prospective freshmen, transfer, and non-traditional students through high school visits, community college visits, college fairs, and com