    "https://jobs.lssu.edu/jobs/gameday-statistician-sault-ste-marie-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Gameday Statistician",
      "description": "Gameday Statistician - Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Gameday Statistician - Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Gameday Statistician Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Administrative Professional Athletics Temporary Part Time Title: Gameday Statistician VP Area: Athletics Department: Athletic Communications Published Salary Range: Up to 20.00 an hour Job Summary/Basic Function: The Gameday Statistician works as part of the official scorers' team for Laker Athletics Events. Employees may work as spotters, official scorekeeper (called \"the book\"), PC input operators for NCAA Live Stats, shot clock operators, and other duties as assigned to the scoring and operation of games. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Live Game Tracking: Attend scheduled games and accurately record real-time statistics for both individual players and the team. Data Entry and Management: Input collected statistics into designated software or databases, ensuring accuracy and integrity of the data. Communication: Effectively communicate statistical insights. Software Proficiency: Utilize relevant sports statistics software for data entry, analysis, and report generation. Rule Familiarity: Maintain a thorough understanding of gameplay rules and statistical scoring regulations. Accuracy and Detail: Demonstrate a high level of attention to detail to ensure the accuracy of all recorded and reported statistics. Timely Reporting: Provide reports and analysis in a timely manner to facilitate effective decision-making. Data Integrity: Ensure the integrity and accuracy of collected data through rigorous quality control processes. Minimum Qualifications: A working knowledge of basketball, hockey, and/or volleyball Strong Communication skills Preferred Qualifications: Familiarity with NCAA rules and terminology is required. Training will be provided as needed, but candidates should possess a basic understanding of NCAA regulations and terminology. Work Hours: Laker Athletics Events. Employees must arrive a minimum of one hour before the start of the event. Apply now! Similar Jobs Regional Recruiter Admissions • Serve as the primary LSSU admissions representative for the assigned regional territory. • Recruit prospective freshmen, transfer, and non-traditional students through high school visits, community college visits, college fairs, and community events. • Build and maintain positive relationships with high school counselors, community college advisors, alumni, and community organizations to promote LSSU. • Conduct individual advising sessions, group presentations, and information sessions to guide students and families through the admissions and financial aid process. • Actively manage territory through a strategic communication plan utilizing multiple platforms, including email, phone, text, social media, and CRM (Slate). • Regularly track and report outreach activities, prospect data, and enrollment trends to inform strategies and assess effectiveness. • Meet established recruitment goals, communication benchmarks, and enrollment targets for the assigned region. • Collaborate with the broader Admissions team to execute university-wide recruitment campaigns and special initiatives. • Organize and host local recruitment events and receptions for prospective and admitted students. • Travel to LSSU’s main campus at least once per quarter. • Other duties as assigned. Regional Recruiter Admissions • Serve as the primary LSSU admissions representative for the assigned regional territory. • Recruit prospective freshmen, transfer, and non-traditional students through high school visits, community college visits, college fairs, and community events. • Build and maintain positive relationships with high school counselors, community college advisors, alumni, and community organizations to promote LSSU. • Conduct individual advising sessions, group presentations, and information sessions to guide students and families through 